#{[17592186516866 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516866 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516866 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516866 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516866 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7d6b312-8b7a-5ed1-a8f0-4e6a0733fe64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516866 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
